    <bpmn:process id="W_W4907" name="W4907. In-Store Media Technology &amp; Integration Architecture" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Platform change; new integration; enterprise-architecture review (VS-113); cyber review (VS-27.3)
Frequency: Per change + periodic architecture review
Volume: 1 in-store-media tech stack × ~205 sites × integrations
Owner: In-Store Media Manager / Enterprise Architecture (VS-113) / IT (VS-27)
Participants: EA (VS-113), IT (VS-27/VS-27.3), Vendor (W4892/W4910), DAM (VS-137), Retail Media (VS-48)
Source: workflow W4907 — In-Store Media Technology &amp; Integration Architecture</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4907_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4907_Lane1" name="EA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4907_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4907_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4907_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W4907_Lane2" name="Cyber">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4907_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4907_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4907_Start4" name="Platform change; new integration; enterprise-architecture review (VS-113); cyber review…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4907_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4907_Task5" name="Design the in-store-media architecture per EA standards (VS-113): the central…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Design the in-store-media architecture per EA standards (VS-113): the central CMS/DAM (VS-137), the store player/edge device model, network/connectivity (VS-27), offline-resilience (local cache), the integrations to POS/price (VS-151), retail-media (VS-48), loyalty/CDP (VS-13/VS-126), store-comms (VS-63), and the emergency-override/fire-panel link (W4902/VS-24)
Responsible (R): EA / IT / In-Store Media Manager
Accountable (A): CIO / VP Marketing
Duration: Per review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4907_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4907_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4907_Task6" name="Secure the stack (VS-27.3/VS-161): signage-player/network segmentation…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Secure the stack (VS-27.3/VS-161): signage-player/network segmentation, firmware-update pipeline (VS-99), vendor cyber attestation (VS-161), and RA 10173 data minimization (signage/footfall/voice); manage as part of the cyber perimeter
Responsible (R): Cyber (VS-27.3) / TPRM (VS-161) / IT
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4907_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4907_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4907_Task7" name="Govern change &amp; standards: new integrations/screens via the EA change process…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Govern change &amp; standards: new integrations/screens via the EA change process (VS-27.1/VS-113), standardize the store AV kit (W4906), and maintain the integration architecture documentation
Responsible (R): EA / IT / In-Store Media Manager
Accountable (A): CIO / VP Marketing
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4907_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4907_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4907_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4907_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-736 (ensure controlled execution — Ambient Media Analytics, Technology &amp; Program Assurance (PA-168.3).) | - CTL-736: EA-approved architecture; cyber-segmentation + firmware + TPRM; offline fallback; change-governed
Owner: In-Store Media Manager / Enterprise Architecture (VS-113) / IT (VS-27)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W4907_Assoc10" sourceRef="W4907_Annotation9" targetRef="W4907_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
